.TH "ONIG" "3" "" "pstring 1.5" "pstring manual"
.SH NAME
onig \- API reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fB#include <onig.h>\fR
.fi
.PP
.nf
\fBstatic const struct pstrexpr_vt pstrexpr_onig_vt;\fR
.fi
.PP
.nf
\fBPSTR_INLINE int pstrexpr_register_onig(const char *prefix);\fR
.fi
.SH REFERENCE
.SS pstrexpr_onig_vt
.PP
The vtable, in case you want to register it under a different name.
.SS pstrexpr_register_onig
.PP
Initializes Oniguruma for UTF\-8 and registers it under \fBprefix\fR,
"onig" if it's \fBNULL\fR. Errors: see \fBpstrexpr_register\fR.
.RS 4
.PP
libonig exports its own POSIX\-style \fBregcomp\fR and \fBregexec\fR. In a program
that links it, these replace the C library's, which silently breaks
\fB<pstring/pattern/posix.h>\fR (it would run Oniguruma's BRE/ERE emulation).
Don't use the two adapters in the same program.
.RE
